From: tangency-labs/smlib 1ed86693f9201019d30319563b2ab16509f02d3e (branch capi-solidcraft)
Subject: SMLib: pointer maps hand out their keys in insertion order, not address order

Cherry-picked onto capi-tess @ 7eba8aa, source part only (the capi README and test hunks of
the original commit do not apply there). SmMapPtrToPtr / SmMapPtrToPtrs (and SmRelation) were
std::unordered_map / unordered_set keyed by pointers and handed out keys, values and pairs in
address order, so SmOffsetExecutive (shell, offset), the fillet executive and the Booleans
depended on the heap layout: the same shell failed with 1001 or 1006 depending on earlier
allocations, natively and in Wasm differently. Lookups stay hashed; iteration follows the
order of first insertion.

